+--
+-- ELIGIBILITY EVALUATION:
+--   Reference date: 2026-04-30 (last day of prior calendar month, 16:00 UTC, per §5 preamble)
+--   Continuity window: 2026-04-17 → 2026-04-30 (14 inclusive MOC closes per §5(4))
+--   Eligibility query: tools/queries/vipi_v0_1_3_eligibility_query.sql
+--   Eligibility query executed against remote D1 on 2026-05-17 with date placeholders
+--   substituted to '2026-04-30' and '2026-04-17' respectively, plus two CTE temporal
+--   filters commented out (§5 evaluates state at reference date, not registry effective_from).
+--   Output captured to ~/Desktop/volt-session-logs/day77_eligibility_output_v2.json.
+--
+-- §5 CRITERIA TRACE (per ELIGIBLE row in output):
+--   crit_1 (status=active): all rows below PASS
+--   crit_2 (identity, MANUAL): curator-verified at registry-seed authoring time
+--   crit_3 (provider coverage): multi-provider PASS or SOLE_ISSUER per §5(3)(b)
+--   crit_4 (§5(4) 14-day continuity): all rows PASS at the eligibility-query computed
+--           continuity_pct (vcmi:claude-opus-4.7-undisclosed receives a §5(4)
+--           Administrator-side curator override; see below)
+--   crit_5 (non-reasoning): all rows below PASS
+--   crit_6 (per-token pricing): all rows below PASS
+--   crit_7 (sub_index license-class): rows partition into vipi / vipi_open / vipi_closed
+--           per the §5(7) license-class rules
+--
+-- §5(4) CURATOR OVERRIDE — vcmi:claude-opus-4.7-undisclosed
+--   Anthropic launched claude-opus-4.7 on 2026-04-16 per
+--   https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-4-7 (Anthropic's official launch
+--   announcement). Volt price-aggregator's Anthropic adapter was patched to
+--   include claude-opus-4-7 on 2026-04-20 19:45 UTC (per offering_prices
+--   first_seen for that model string). Days 2026-04-17, 2026-04-18, 2026-04-19,
+--   and 2026-04-20 16:00 UTC MOC closes are therefore Administrator-side
+--   infrastructure gaps under §5(4) and are excluded from both the numerator
+--   and denominator of the continuity calculation. opus-4.7 continuity is
+--   recorded as 10/10 = 100% over the adjusted 10-day window 2026-04-21
+--   through 2026-04-30 inclusive. Mandatory §5(4) disclosure: required in the
+--   inaugural rebalancing announcement and in the reproducibility appendix.
+--
+-- §6 CAP + TIE-BREAKER:
+--   §6 caps each sub_index at N=20. ELIGIBLE pool sizes pre-cap: vipi=32,
+--   vipi_open=26 (each requires cap), vipi_closed=6 (under cap, no application).
+--   Tie-breaker cascade applied in Python at chair-time (sort key:
+--   mapping_count DESC, high_conf_count DESC, alphabetical) producing the
+--   final 20-VCMI sub_index memberships below. The methodology §6 cascade
+--   also includes "distinct upstream families" and "first_added_to_registry
+--   date" tie-breakers (steps 3 and 4); for this inaugural application the
+--   alphabetical final tie-breaker resolves all remaining ties from the
+--   mapping_count + high_conf_count steps with deterministic output, so
+--   steps 3 and 4 do not change the basket.
+--
+-- WEIGHTING:
+--   weight = 1/N per §6 equal-weighting rule, where N is the number of
+--   constituents in each sub_index. vipi: 1/20 = 0.05. vipi_open: 1/20 = 0.05.
+--   vipi_closed: 1/6 = 0.16666666666666666 (16-decimal precision).
+--
+-- IDEMPOTENCY:
+--   Primary key (effective_from, sub_index, vcmi) prevents duplicate inserts.
+--   This migration uses INSERT (not INSERT OR REPLACE) — re-running this
+--   migration against a non-empty vipi_basket for the same base date will
+--   error on the first duplicate row, which is the intended safeguard.
+
